            {
                id defects.ffi-string-free-cross-heap
                title "Per-module mw_string_free routing is unenforced across wasm heaps"
                priority 1
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T18:00:18.55352Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Investigated; no runtime check is possible and none was invented. Inside a wasm module a pointer is just an offset into that module's linear memory, so an offset minted by another module is indistinguishable from a native one. Two candidate defences were considered and rejected as weaker than they look: an address registry (offsets collide across modules with high probability, turning a cross-heap free into a double-free of the checking module's own live allocation) and a magic-header canary (needs hand-rolled alloc/dealloc in four crates and breaks the documented CString::into_raw contract). What landed is documentation only — the rewritten rule plus per-module Safety docs stating that mw_string_free validates nothing beyond null, and a comment at the actual enforcement point in web/index.template.html. The pairing is correct today by encapsulation rather than enforcement: loadRenderer's closure allocates, reads and frees resultPtr against its own module and never hands the pointer out. Nothing stops a future caller, and since every module exports the symbol under the same name a crossed call would link and run rather than fail. Two genuine fixes exist, both changing the exported C ABI and so out of this node's scope: unique per-module free symbols (mw_render_graphviz_string_free etc.), making an accidental cross-call a missing-export error; or module-owned buffers, removing host ownership entirely. Either requires bumping ffi.render-shim.lazy-module, editing three build.rs export lists and the frontend, and rebuilding the emscripten artifacts. Node stays open pending that decision."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T19:06:00.095011Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Resolved by making the free symbol engine-qualified per lazily-loaded module: mw_render_graphviz_string_free, mw_render_pikchr_string_free, mw_render_typst_string_free. A plugin-to-plugin or core-pointer-to-plugin crossing is now an unresolvable symbol — an emscripten ccall resolution throw — rather than a silent cross-heap free. The two primary modules (markdawn-wasm-emscripten and the markdawn-swift staticlib) deliberately keep the unqualified mw_string_free: the Swift side has a single allocator and no second heap, and it is published ABI declared in include/markdawn.h, the three xcframework headers and Markdawn.swift, so renaming would be churn with no safety delta. The asymmetry is now itself the signal — unprefixed means core heap, mw_render_<engine>_ prefixed means that plugin's heap. One crossing remains expressible and is still held by encapsulation only: handing a render module's pointer to the core module's mw_string_free, which cannot happen today because a render module's raw pointer never leaves loadRenderer's closure. DEPLOYMENT: the emscripten artifacts are gitignored build outputs and could not be rebuilt in this environment. web/markdawn_render_{graphviz,pikchr,typst}.js and their .wasm still export the old mw_string_free, and web/index.html must be regenerated from index.template.html. Until that rebuild happens the checked-in template names symbols the stale artifacts do not export, so diagram rendering throws at the free call — the intended failure mode, but the demo page is broken until the artifacts are regenerated."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T19:06:03.76415Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T21:48:25.018984Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Correction to the deployment caveat in the previous note: the emscripten artifacts HAVE now been rebuilt. emcc was available via Homebrew and both wasm targets were installed, so the four release builds ran and web/markdawn_render_{graphviz,pikchr,typst}.{js,wasm} plus markdawn_wasm_emscripten.{js,wasm} were regenerated, and web/index.html was rebuilt from index.template.html. Verified: each render module exports mw_render_<engine>_string_free with zero remaining references to the old mw_string_free, and the core module retains the generic name as designed. The demo page works again. Caveat that still stands: these artifacts are gitignored build outputs, so they are not in the commit — any other checkout or CI job needs crates/markdawn-wasm-emscripten/serve.sh (or the equivalent build+copy steps) run once before the demo page will load, otherwise it will throw at the free call against stale artifacts."
                        after_done true
                    }
                )
            }

