                    }
                )
            }

            {
                id defects.spec-bodies-inaccurate
                title "Four rule bodies describe behaviour the code does not have"
                priority 1
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-07-29T22:38:37.799129Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Found while closing defects.test-coverage-gaps: four rule bodies assert things the implementation does not do. Each was caught by someone trying to write the test the rule implies and finding it fail.\n\n1. core.error.location — says byte_offset is \"an offset into the parser's normalized buffer — after line-ending and tab normalization\". Both halves false. Every top-level InlineParser is constructed with base_offset: 0 (src/parser.rs:1979, :5300), so the offset is relative to the containing block's inline run, not the buffer — a CRLF document with an error on line 3 reports offset 1 where the normalized-buffer offset is 6. And normalize_chunk (src/parser.rs:2253) maps only NUL to U+FFFD and CR/CRLF to LF; there is no tab normalization anywhere. Left impl-only rather than annotated, because a verify site would attest to a contract the code does not honour.\n\n2. editing.serialize.round-trip v1 — one clause stale: \"Subscript and Superscript come back as Html\". They do not. promote_semantic_html (src/parser.rs:1993) unconditionally promotes <sub>/<sup> back to Node::Subscript/Superscript, so they round-trip faithfully. Every other documented loss in that rule was verified and is real.\n\n3. iced.hit-test.outside-glyphs — the bidi clause is wrong. It says a point right of every glyph is the logical end of the line's byte coverage \"under LTR, RTL and mixed-bidi layout alike\". For a pure-RTL line, buffer().hit(5000, y) resolves to 0 — the logical start. The LTR clauses are all verified and correct.\n\n4. iced.renderer.parse-failure-empty — describes dead code, not merely hard-to-reach code. Renderer::render builds its own parser with no extensions and no max_input_bytes, and the only three Error variants a parse can yield are InputTooLarge (needs a cap), InvalidExtensionMatch (needs an extension) and MalformedEventStream (an Option::ok_or on str::chars().next() that cannot fire for valid UTF-8). The Err(_) => column![] arm is unreachable under the public API. Either the rule should say so, or the arm should go.\n\nFixing these means rewriting the bodies and bumping versions; for (4) it may mean deleting code instead."
                    }
                )
            }

            {
